course: everyday
lesson: 460
title: The pet that loves you most
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When Sam's grandad goes into hospital, Grandad's old Labrador Bramble comes to stay. Every evening she lies across Sam's bedroom door like a furry draught excluder. When Sam cries about Grandad, she puts her heavy grey chin on his lap and just stays there. She never judges, never tells. Grandad gets better and Bramble goes home, but whenever Sam visits she skids down the hall to him, tail going like a windscreen wiper.
explain: Chloe's guinea pigs squeak like a car alarm every morning when she comes downstairs. «They know your footsteps,» says Mum. On holiday the neighbour feeds them, and they don't squeak once. Lily's goldfish Bubbles swims to the front of the tank for her, but not for her brother — fish learn who feeds them. Jake's dog Diesel is huge and scruffy and everyone crosses the road, but with Jake he's a big softie who sleeps on his feet. On a bad day Jake takes Diesel for a long walk instead of shouting at anyone, and comes back calmer.
explain: Pets depend on you completely. Maddie forgets to fill the rabbit's water bowl for two days and finds it lying still in the hutch. Mum rushes it to the vet; it has fluids and lives, but the vet says one more day could have been too late. Maddie makes a chart and ticks it every single day. Sam's dog Scout slips out of a gate left open and Sam searches for hours with a torch until a neighbour finds him two streets away. The latch gets fixed and Scout gets microchipped.
explain: Lily's goldfish dies after three years. «It's only a fish, get another one, lol,» says Kieran. Lily buries Bubbles in the garden under a painted stone, and she is properly gutted — very upset. Connor's family can't keep Bruno any more, with a new baby and a tiny flat, so Bruno goes to a friend's farm; Connor visits twice a year and Bruno goes wild with joy every time. Sometimes the kind choice is the hard one. Love doesn't stop with a move. Some love is odd: Kieran's cat leaves a dead mouse on his pillow as a present, and Mum clears it up with a bag. When Mia has flu, her grandma's old cat doesn't leave her bed for three days.
fact: Pets can be a real comfort when you are sad, scared or ill.
fact: The pet that loves you most is usually the one you look after yourself every day.
fact: Many animals, even fish and guinea pigs, learn to recognise the person who feeds them.
fact: Pets depend on you completely for food and water; a small animal without water can become dangerously ill within a day or two.
fact: A chart or routine helps you remember to check water and food every day.
fact: Keep gates and doors shut, and make sure pets are microchipped and wear a tag with a phone number in case they get lost.
fact: When a pet dies, it is normal to be very sad; a good friend says «sorry about your pet», not «get another one».
fact: Sometimes a family cannot keep a pet, and finding it a good new home is a kind choice, not a betrayal.
fact: Cats sometimes bring dead mice or birds as «presents»; an adult should remove them with gloves or a bag, and the cat should not be punished.
fact: Walking a dog can help you calm down when you are angry.
fact: Animals often notice when someone is unwell, but you should still wash your hands and not let pets lick your face.
fact: «Gutted» is British slang for very disappointed or upset.
exercise: What did Bramble do when Sam cried about Grandad? | Put her head on his lap and stayed | Barked loudly at him until he stopped crying | Ran off to find Grandad | Hid in the garden shed
exercise: Why do Chloe's guinea pigs squeak when she comes downstairs? | They know her footsteps and she feeds them | They are frightened of her and want to hide away | They squeak for anyone at all | They are too cold at night
exercise: Why didn't the guinea pigs squeak for the neighbour? | They didn't know the neighbour's footsteps | The neighbour was too quiet coming into the room | Guinea pigs only squeak at night | They had lost their voices
exercise: Does a goldfish know who feeds it? | Yes, fish can learn who feeds them | No, fish forget in three seconds | Only if it's a very big fish | No, fish can't see outside water
exercise: How does Diesel help Jake on a bad day? | A long walk with him calms Jake down | Diesel growls at Jake's teachers until they stop | Diesel does Jake's homework | Diesel keeps Jake indoors
exercise: What nearly happened to Maddie's rabbit? | It nearly died from no water | It ran away into the woods | It ate the whole hutch | It got too fat to move
exercise: What did Maddie do so it wouldn't happen again? | Made a chart and checked every day | Gave the rabbit to her nan to look after | Filled the bowl once a month | Asked the rabbit to remind her
exercise: How did Scout the dog get lost? | The gate was left open | He was stolen by a fox at night | He jumped out of the window | He followed the bin lorry
exercise: What helps a lost pet get home? | A microchip and a tag with a phone number | A shiny new collar with a bell but no name tag | A photo on your bedroom wall | A loud squeaky toy
exercise: Kieran said «it's only a fish, get another one». What would a good friend say? | «Sorry about Bubbles» | «Fish don't count anyway» | «Stop crying, it's a fish» | «Good, it smelled of pond»
exercise: Why did Bruno go to live on a farm? | The family had a new baby and a small flat | Bruno bit the new baby | Connor didn't love him any more after he grew up | Farms pay for dogs
exercise: Was rehoming Bruno a betrayal? | No, it was a kind choice for him | Yes, families must keep pets forever | Yes, Bruno will forget them | No, because dogs hate flats
exercise: Kieran's cat leaves a dead mouse on his pillow. Why? | It's a «present» to someone she cares about | She wants Kieran to cook it for her dinner tonight | She's angry at Kieran | She's trying to scare him off
exercise: What should happen to the dead mouse? | An adult removes it with gloves or a bag | Kieran picks it up with bare hands | The cat gets punished | Leave it there for a week
exercise: Mia's grandma's cat sleeps on Mia when she has flu. What should Mia still do? | Wash her hands and not let it lick her face | Let it lick her face all day, since cats are clean | Keep it under the covers all week | Give it her medicine
exercise: «Lily's properly gutted.» What does «gutted» mean? | Very upset | Very hungry indeed | Very lucky today | Very tired and sleepy
test: «guinea pigs are thick, they don't know who u are». Are they? | No, they learn who feeds them | Yes, they know nobody | Yes, they think everyone is food | No, they know everyone's name
test: Maddie: «the rabbit's fine, it can go a few days without water». What would most likely happen? | It could become dangerously ill | It would be totally fine | It would drink rainwater | It would learn to need less
test: Your mate leaves the garden gate open «just for a sec». Your dog's in the garden. What's the risk? | The dog could get out and get lost | The dog will tidy the garden | Nothing, dogs never leave their own gardens | The gate will rust
test: «my cat brought me a dead bird, i'm gonna ground her». Better idea? | Don't punish her, an adult clears it up | Make her eat it in front of you so she learns | Lock her in a cupboard | Give the bird back to her
test: In a cartoon the family's dog finds its way home across the whole country by itself. What's the safer real-life plan? | Microchip, tag and keep gates shut | Trust the dog to find home | Draw a map for the dog | Never let the dog outside at all
test: Connor's mate: «you gave your dog away? that's cold, bruv». What's the truth? | Finding him a good home was the kind choice | Connor never really cared about him at all | Bruno will forget Connor at once | Dogs should never be rehomed
test: Lily's still sad about Bubbles a week later. Kieran: «move on, it's a fish». Who's being fair? | Lily, it's normal to grieve a pet | Kieran, fish don't count | Kieran, a week is far too long to be sad | Nobody, she should buy two fish
test: Jake's had a horrible day and wants to punch a wall. What does the lesson suggest? | Take the dog for a long walk | Shout at the dog | Lock himself in his room for a week | Find someone to fight
test: What would happen if no one fed Chloe's guinea pigs while she was away? | They'd become ill and could die | They'd find food in the garden | They'd be fine for a month | They'd squeak until the food came
test: Which pet is most likely to love you most? | The one you feed and look after yourself | The one you buy the most toys and treats for | The biggest pet in the house | The one you hug the hardest
exam: Identify the principal reason for which a pet may show particular attachment to one member of a household. | That member provides its daily care | That member is the youngest in the household | That member possesses the largest bedroom | That member is the most frequently absent
exam: Given that a small domestic animal has been deprived of water for two days, ascertain the most appropriate course of action. | To seek immediate veterinary attention | To wait a further day to observe developments | To provide food alone, but no water at all | To return the animal to its hutch untreated
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the rehoming of a pet when a family can no longer keep it? | It may constitute a kind and responsible decision | It invariably amounts to a betrayal of the animal | It causes the animal to forget its family immediately | It is prohibited in all circumstances
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning measures to secure the return of a lost dog. | Microchipping and a tag bearing a telephone number | Reliance upon the dog's sense of direction alone | The display of the dog's photograph indoors | The purchase of an untagged collar
